    <p class="para lt-chem-349739">Write an expression for the initial rate of decrease of [I<sub>3</sub><sup>&minus;</sup>], &Delta;[I<sub>3</sub><sup>&minus;</sup>]/&Delta;<em>t</em>. When the reaction rate of the forward reaction is equal to that of the reverse reaction: <em>k</em><sub>f</sub>/<em>k</em><sub>r</sub> = [H<sub>3</sub>AsO<sub>3</sub>][I<sub>3</sub><sup>&minus;</sup>]/[H<sub>3</sub>AsO<sub>4</sub>][I<sup>&minus;</sup>]<sup>3</sup>[H<sup>+</sup>]<sup>2</sup>. Based on this information, what can you say about the nature of the rate-determining steps for the reverse and the forward reactions?</p>
    </div>
    </li>
</ol>
</div></div>

